<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 111,860 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 111,860 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 111,860 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday compared to 88,115 tonnes in the same period on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Saturday    March 14</p>
<p>    Export cargo		27,995	26,746</p>
<p>    Import cargo		83,865	61,369</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and nine are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasen Courage    15/3</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-I	    15/3</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Vigour		 17/3</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Ying Song Hu	 19/3</p>
<p>Containers		  240	 Dammam Bay	   19/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	 Lapanto Glory	20/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
